.\" help2man include for imud-imutest.8 — the hand-written sections.
.\" OPTIONS is generated from `imud-imutest --help`; everything else lives here.
.\" See tools/man-postprocess.py and `make docs-man`.

[NAME]
imud\-imutest \- validate an imud sensor driver against real hardware

[SYNOPSIS]
.B imud-imutest
\&[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\&[\fB\-\-report\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\&[\fIdevice overrides\fR]
\&[\fIphases\fR]
\&[\fItuning\fR]

[DESCRIPTION]
.B imud-imutest
drives a registered IMU and magnetometer driver through the whole
.BR imu_ops_t / mag_ops_t
contract on real silicon, and writes a Markdown report suitable for pasting
into a bug report.
.PP
A driver's register map is checked against the datasheet when it is written,
and the in-tree unit tests prove its register encoding and decoding against a
mock I2C bus. Neither says anything about timing, real output rate, FIFO or
interrupt behaviour, or whether the chip-to-board axis remap is correct. This
tool covers that gap.
.PP
Drivers that have never run on physical hardware are marked
.B experimental
in the registry, and
.BR imud (8)
warns at startup when one is selected. A clean report from this tool is what
justifies clearing that flag \(em see
.B REPORT
below.
.PP
It works with any registered driver, not only the one in the configuration
file: use the device overrides to point it at whatever is wired up.

[PHASES]
.TP
.B Passive
No operator action. Chip identification, reset timing, control-register
readback, measured output rate against the rate the driver reports it will
program,
FIFO depth, deliberate overflow and recovery, sequence-number monotonicity and
gaps, the error-return contract, noise floor, gravity magnitude, temperature
sanity, hardware-timestamp rate and wrap handling, interrupt edge counting, and
a full-scale sweep that re-initialises the part at every advertised range. The
accelerometer arm of that sweep is graded against gravity; the gyroscope arm is
recorded but not graded, because a stationary gyro reads about zero at every
range and its noise floor only tracks full scale when quantisation dominates
it.
.TP
.B Six-face
Prompts for each of six orientations and checks that the axis pointing down
reads \-g and the axis pointing up reads +g, in the NED board frame (X forward,
Y starboard, Z down). This is the check that catches an inverted or swapped
axis, the most likely defect in a new driver.
.TP
.B Gyro rotation
Prompts for a deliberate turn about each axis and checks the sign follows the
right-hand rule, and that the integrated angle is the right order of magnitude.
A hand turn is only good to about ten percent, so this catches factor errors \(em
notably returning degrees per second where the contract requires radians \(em
rather than measuring sensitivity. The sign check fails outright when the turn
integrates to less than a quarter of the commanded angle: the sign of a value
near zero carries no information, so a gyro that is not responding must not
score a pass on it.
.TP
.B Magnetometer spin
Prompts for two slow level circles and checks the field magnitude, that every
axis responds, that the heading circle is covered, and \(em the substantive
check \(em that the magnetometer's heading turns the same way and by the same
amount as the gyroscope's Z integral. A disagreement there means the mag axes
are inverted or swapped relative to the IMU.

[REPORT]
The report is self-contained and prints every threshold inline, so a reviewer
never needs the source to know what a check asserted. It records the
environment, the driver's advertised capabilities, one row per check with the
measured and expected values and a one-line diagnosis, an appendix of raw
measurements, and the command line that produced it.
.PP
Results are graded:
.TP
.B PASS
The driver met the contract.
.TP
.B FAIL
The driver violated the contract on evidence the bench cannot explain away.
.TP
.B WARN
Out of band, but with a plausible physical cause \(em an unlevel surface, a
moving board, magnetic clutter, a starved scheduler \(em or a check that is
one-sided by nature. A warning never blocks clearing the experimental flag; it
asks the reviewer to read the number.
.TP
.B SKIP
Capability absent, phase not selected, prerequisite failed, or a resource was
unavailable.
.TP
.B INFO
Recorded for the record, with no pass criterion.
.PP
Three limits are stated in every report rather than left implicit. The
control-register diff is raw and undecoded by design, because deciding whether
those values are correct needs the datasheet. The registers excluded from that
diff as volatile are found by experiment \(em the mapped range is read several
times with the part running and no writes in between \(em so a register that
happens to hold the same value through every pass is not caught, and every
report prints how many were excluded and how many compared. And the requirement
that
.B \-1
is returned
.I only
on a genuine I2C fault is checked off-hardware by the unit tests, which inject
bus failures through the mock; a hardware run can only show that no spurious
errors occurred.

[EXIT STATUS]
.TP
.B 0
Every check passed.
.TP
.B 1
Usage, configuration, or I/O error; also when the daemon is running and
.B \-\-force
was not given.
.TP
.B 2
At least one check failed.
.TP
.B 3
Warnings only.
.TP
.B 130
Aborted by the operator.

[FILES]
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud.conf
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I ./imud-imutest-<driver>-<timestamp>.md
Default report path.

[NOTES]
The daemon
.RB ( imud )
and
.B imud-imutest
must not run simultaneously. Both open the same I2C device and, more
importantly, both drain the same FIFO, so each would see roughly half the
samples: the measured output rate reads low and the sequence-gap check fails
for a reason that has nothing to do with the driver. The tool refuses to start
when it can reach the daemon's status socket.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl stop imud
imud-imutest --imu-driver icm20948 --mag-driver ak09916 --mag-addr 0x0C --all
sudo systemctl start imud
.EE
.RE
.PP
The tool can also be run against the
.B sim
driver, which has a real FIFO, sequence counter and timestamp. That exercises
the tool itself rather than any hardware; the report says so and never
recommends clearing an experimental flag.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-imutest --imu-driver sim --mag-driver sim --passive
.EE
.RE

[SEE ALSO]
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud-cal (8),
.BR imud-mon (1),
.BR imud.conf (5)

